<details><summary><a href='https://github.com/code-review-benchmark/keycloak__keycloak__qodo__PR37429__20260123/pull/1/files#diff-c9b90df19d737df4f7062b741b1d0f7e01d2afe3bed28afd6792012a3a412b18R145-R162'><strong>Possible Issue</strong></a>

Anchor-tag validation/sanitization mutates the input string while iterating with a Matcher created from the original value, which can lead to missed matches or incorrect behavior in multi-anchor strings. Also, the current logic validates anchors only in a strict sequential match; ensure this is intended and robust for repeated/duplicated anchors and different ordering scenarios.
</summary>

```java
private static final Pattern ANCHOR_PATTERN = Pattern.compile("</?a[^>]*>");

/**
 * Allow only those anchor tags from the source key to also appear in the target key.
 */
private String santizeAnchors(String key, String value, String englishValue) {
    Matcher matcher = ANCHOR_PATTERN.matcher(value);
    Matcher englishMatcher = ANCHOR_PATTERN.matcher(englishValue);
    while (matcher.find()) {
        if (englishMatcher.find() && Objects.equals(matcher.group(), englishMatcher.group())) {
            value = value.replaceFirst(Pattern.quote(englishMatcher.group()), "");
        } else {
            messages.add("Didn't find anchor tag " + matcher.group() + " in original string");
            break;
        }
    }
    return value;
}
```

</details>

<details><summary><a href='https://github.com/code-review-benchmark/keycloak__keycloak__qodo__PR37429__20260123/pull/1/files#diff-c9b90df19d737df4f7062b741b1d0f7e01d2afe3bed28afd6792012a3a412b18R73-R87'><strong>Robustness</strong></a>

English bundle resolution is based on regex replaceAll on absolute paths and then unconditionally opened. This can be brittle across different directory layouts and locale naming patterns and may fail with unexpected file names. Consider validating file existence and using safer locale/path derivation to avoid false failures or mis-resolving the English source file.
</summary>

