[**Logic**] When V2 FGAP is enabled, `canMapRoles()` now returns `hasPermission(client, MAP_ROLES)` only. That unintentionally removes the previous fallback that allowed administrators holding `manage-clients` (or any broader `canManage(client)` capability) to keep mapping roles even when no explicit authorization policy exists. As soon as FGAP v2 is turned on, existing admins will start getting `403` on any role-mapping operation until custom permissions are created for every client, which is a regression from the legacy behavior.

Bring back the earlier short-circuit so that high-privilege admins keep their abilities, and only fall back to the fine-grained permission when that is not the case:
```suggestion
    @Override
    public boolean canMapRoles(ClientModel client) {
        return canManage(client) || hasPermission(client, AdminPermissionsSchema.MAP_ROLES);
    }
```
The same pattern should apply to `canMapCompositeRoles` and `canMapClientScopeRoles`, otherwise those admin flows are also broken.

