`AdminPermissionsSchema.SCHEMA.getResourceTypeResource(...)` can return `null` (e.g., if the resource store does not yet contain the "Clients" resource). The returned value is immediately assigned to `resource` and then passed to `findByResource(server, resource)` on the very next line without any null guard, which will throw a `NullPointerException` at runtime.

```suggestion
        if (resource == null) {
            // check if there is permission for "all-clients". If so, load its resource and proceed with evaluation
            resource = AdminPermissionsSchema.SCHEMA.getResourceTypeResource(session, server, AdminPermissionsSchema.CLIENTS_RESOURCE_TYPE);

            if (resource == null || authz.getStoreFactory().getPolicyStore().findByResource(server, resource).isEmpty()) {
                return false;
            }
        }
```

