If the commit_function call on line 287 succeeds but any of the mark_committed calls on line 289 fail, the offsets will be committed to Kafka but not marked as committed in the local tracker. This creates an inconsistency where the tracker will attempt to commit these offsets again on the next iteration. While Kafka commits are idempotent, this could lead to unnecessary retry overhead and potential tracking issues. Consider calling commit_function after all mark_committed calls succeed, or wrap the mark_committed calls in their own try-except to handle failures individually.
```suggestion
