**Missing double-check after acquiring write lock**

This implementation of the double-checked locking pattern is incomplete. After releasing the read lock (line 43) and before acquiring the write lock (line 48), another goroutine may have already populated `entryPointAssetsCache`. Without re-checking the cache under the write lock, all goroutines that raced past the `RLock` check with a nil cache will each independently read from disk/CDN and overwrite the cache — defeating the purpose of the pattern.

The standard double-checked locking pattern requires a second check after the write lock is acquired:

```go
entryPointAssetsCacheMu.Lock()
defer entryPointAssetsCacheMu.Unlock()

// Re-check: another goroutine may have already populated the cache between
// the RUnlock above and this Lock.
if cfg.Env != setting.Dev && entryPointAssetsCache != nil {
    return entryPointAssetsCache, nil
}
```

Without this guard, under concurrent load at startup (when the cache is nil), every goroutine that saw a nil cache will redundantly call `readWebAssetsFromFile` or `readWebAssetsFromCDN` and then overwrite the cached result.

