The `align-items` mixin incorrectly passes modern flexbox values (like `flex-start`, `flex-end`) directly to `-webkit-box-align`, which expects legacy syntax values (`start`, `end`, `center`, `baseline`, `stretch`). This will cause silent failures in older webkit implementations. For example, `@include align-items(flex-start)` will not work correctly with `-webkit-box-align: flex-start` as it expects just `start`.

Recommend adding value translation logic:
```scss
@mixin align-items($alignment) {
  $legacy-alignment: $alignment;
  @if $alignment == 'flex-start' { $legacy-alignment: start; }
  @if $alignment == 'flex-end' { $legacy-alignment: end; }

  -webkit-box-align: $legacy-alignment;
  -webkit-align-items: $alignment;
  -ms-flex-align: $alignment;
  align-items: $alignment;
}
```
Or remove legacy prefixes entirely and rely on autoprefixer.

