The `catch` block discards the actual `err` object, so any email delivery failure (SMTP misconfiguration, rate-limit, invalid recipient, etc.) will silently produce just the string `"Error sending AddGuestsEmails"` in logs with no diagnostic information. This makes production debugging effectively impossible.

